  "problem": "Given that $r(t)=\u27e8{2}^{t-1},\\,\\frac{4}{t+1}\u27e9,$ what is $|r(1)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|r(1)|=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Evaluating the function at $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =\u27e8{2}^{0},\\,\\frac{4}{2}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e81,\\,2\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(1)| & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
